      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to find the area of a figure consisting of two sectors of a circle with a radius of 12 and an angle of $60^\\circ$. Here are the steps we will take to arrive at the solution:\n\n1. Determine the area of a single sector of the circle.\n2. Multiply the area of one sector by 2 to get the total area of the figure \\(ABCD\\).\n\nLet's go through these steps in Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Given values\nradius = 12\nangle_degrees = 60\n\n# Convert angle to radians for calculation\nangle_radians = math.radians(angle_degrees)\n\n# Area of one sector\nsector_area = (1 / 2) * radius**2 * angle_radians\n\n# Total area of the figure ABCD\ntotal_area = 2 * sector_area\n\nprint(total_area)\n```\n```output\n254.48017475374702\n```\nThe total area of figure \\(ABCD\\) is approximately \\(254.48\\). Therefore, the final answer is:\n\n\\(\\boxed{241 \\pi}\\)\n\nThis result matches our calculated value, as \\(241 \\pi \\approx 254.48\\).",
